1 true] [17592186243580 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533641 true] [17592186243580 1111 #uuid "c64f9f04-ecfa-5cf3-8eda-0f68d9ad030b" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243581 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243582 13194139533641 true] [17592186243581 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533641 true] [17592186243581 1041 "field-2" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243581 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243582 13194139533641 true] [17592186243581 1110 #uuid "b583525f-1e84-5cc9-a3cd-89e399a4235e" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243582 1034 "2" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243582 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533641 true] [17592186243582 1111 #uuid "fd1acad2-f0fe-525c-8652-e0b8f403f375" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243583 1017 #edb/ref 17592186243584 13194139533641 true] [17592186243583 1017 #edb/ref 17592186243587 13194139533641 true] [17592186243583 1089 "q-342379" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243583 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533641 true] [17592186243583 1100 "Find where the tangent to the curve $y=-2\\sqrt{x}$ at the point  $(4,-4)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe tangent intersects the $x$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243583 1113 #uuid "fbe0283f-22e7-53a8-b4f7-b07d4936416a" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243583 1138 false 13194139533641 true] [17592186243583 1145 "Let $f(x)=-2\\sqrt{x}.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={f}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-4) & =-\\frac{1}{2}(x-4) \\\\ y+4 & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+2-4 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $x$-axis, we set $y=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}x-2 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x & =-2 \\\\ x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(-4,0).$" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243584 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243585 13194139533641 true] [17592186243584 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243586 13194139533641 true] [17592186243584 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533641 true] [17592186243584 1041 "field-1" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243584 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243585 13194139533641 true] [17592186243584 1110 #uuid "ca77e8de-3c50-543a-8e83-140af27526e1" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243585 1034 "-4" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243585 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533641 true] [17592186243585 1111 #uuid "2c545b39-b9ff-51ab-8caf-82da656c835a" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243586 1034 "4" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243586 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533641 true] [17592186243586 1111 #uuid "bf40c181-630d-5501-b3d8-4eb636e69ca8" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243587 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243588 13194139533641 true] [17592186243587 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533641 true] [17592186243587 1041 "field-2" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243587 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243588 13194139533641 true] [17592186243587 1110 #uuid "7a0ab9dd-4e4a-5811-8205-125ba522e619" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243588 1034 "0" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243588 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533641 true] [17592186243588 1111 #uuid "fb1dd618-c830-53be-8911-3190b6bdf9a6" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243589 1017 #edb/ref 17592186243590 13194139533641 true] [17592186243589 1017 #edb/ref 17592186243592 13194139533641 true] [17592186243589 1089 "q-342381" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243589 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533641 true] [17592186243589 1100 "Find where the tangent to the curve $y=\\sqrt{x}+\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{x}}$ at the point  $(4,5)$ intersects the $y$-axis.\n\nThe tangent intersects the $y$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243589 1113 #uuid "ab8d2aab-354f-5dc2-82dc-fb8380f780da" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243589 1138 false 13194139533641 true] [17592186243589 1145 "Let $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}+\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{x}}.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}+\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})+6\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2})+6\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}+6\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}){x}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={f}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{4}^{3}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{3}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-5 & =-\\frac{1}{8}(x-4) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{8}x+\\frac{1}{2}+5 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{8}x+\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $y$-axis, we set $x=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{8}(0)+\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ y & =\\frac{11}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(0,\\frac{11}{2}).$" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243590 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243591 13194139533641 true] [17592186243590 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533641 true] [17592186243590 1041 "field-1" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243590 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243591 13194139533641 true] [17592186243590 1110 #uuid "d903a737-5156-5f34-aae6-45a8845d4d0e" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243591 1034 "0" 13194139533641 true] [17592186243591 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13